The   driver   supports  the  Triones/Highpoint  HPT366,  HPT370,
HPT370A, HPT372 and HPT374 IDE controllers, and provides the  in‐
terface with the hardware for the driver.  The 0x0002 flag forces
the  driver  to  disable DMA on chipsets for which DMA would nor‐
mally be enabled.  This can be used as a  debugging  aid,  or  to
work  around problems where the IDE controller is wired up to the
system incorrectly.  The timings used for the PIO and  DMA  modes
for  controllers  listed above are for a PCI bus running at 30 or
33 MHz.  This driver may not work properly  on  overclocked  sys‐
tems.
